The ready frontier is derived from hard dependencies, passed or waived gates,
resolved structured blockers, and reciprocal plan/task links. It is not
permission or priority. Dates remain audit, freshness, expiry, or explicit
external-constraint data and never select the next task.

`validate.py --check` is read-only and never executes project test, lint,
build, or closure hooks. Those hooks begin `not_assessed`. Project owners must
configure safe argv contracts or record an owned `not_applicable` rationale;
configured hooks run only through the explicit project-check evidence writer
after authority for declared side effects is confirmed. Structural success,
harness adoption, and target-project readiness are separate conclusions.
